225: \section{Command Line Parameters Reference}
226: \label{sec:parameters}
227: % ======================================================================
228: 
229: The \code{compass\_sim} simulator provides a highly configurable interface. The parameters are categorized into six functional groups:
230: 
231: \subsection{Lattice Geometry Options}
232: These options configure the spatial dimensions and layout of the needle array:
233: \begin{description}
234:     \item[\code{--N <int>}] Number of rows in the lattice grid. Default: \code{8}.
235:     \item[\code{--M <int>}] Number of columns in the lattice grid. Default: \code{8}.
236:     \item[\code{--R <float>}] Radius of the circumscribed circle enclosing each needle (\si{m}). The center-to-center separation distance between nearest neighbor needles is $2R$. Default: \code{0.025} (\si{2.5\ cm}).
237:     \item[\code{--needle\_frac <float>}] Fractional needle length relative to cell diameter $2R$, bounded in $[0.0, 0.8]$. The physical needle length is $L = 2R \cdot \text{needle\_frac}$. Default: \code{0.80}. Values outside this range are clamped.
238:     \item[\code{--geometry \{square,triangular,honeycomb\}}] The physical layout structure of the grid. Default: \code{square}.
239: \end{description}
240: 
241: \subsection{Physics \& Material Properties}
242: These parameters dictate the mechanical and magnetic properties of individual needles, integration time step constraints, and boundary conditions:
243: \begin{description}
244:     \item[\code{--moment <float>}] Magnetic moment $m$ of each needle (\si{A.m^2}). If omitted, it is calculated from the steel volume ($L \times w \times d$) magnetized to saturation.
245:     \item[\code{--inertia <float>}] Physical moment of inertia $I$ (\si{kg.m^2}) of each needle. If omitted, it is computed assuming a uniform thin rectangular sheet rotating about its center.
246:     \item[\code{--pivot\_radius <float>}] Radius of the cylindrical pivot at the center of the needle (\si{m}). Default: \code{0.0} (no pivot).
247:     \item[\code{--pivot\_thickness <float>}] Thickness/height of the cylindrical pivot (\si{m}). Default: \code{0.0}.
248:     \item[\code{--pivot\_density <float>}] Density of the pivot material (\si{kg/m^3}). Default: \code{8500.0} (brass).
249:     \item[\code{--pivot\_mass <float>}] Explicit mass of the central pivot (\si{kg}). If supplied, it overrides density and dimension calculations.
250:     \item[\code{--needle\_thickness <float>}] Thickness $d$ of the needle sheet (\si{m}). Used for moment/inertia auto-calibration. Default: \code{0.0004} (\si{0.40\ mm}).
251:     \item[\code{--steel\_density <float>}] Density of the needle material (\si{kg/m^3}). Default: \code{7850.0} (carbon steel).
252:     \item[\code{--steel\_Bsat <float>}] Saturation magnetic flux density $B_{\text{sat}}$ (\si{T}). Default: \code{2.0}. Used for calculating magnetic moment ($M_s = B_{\text{sat}} / \mu_0$).
253:     \item[\code{--damping <float>}] Viscous damping coefficient $b$ (\si{N.m.s/rad}). Controls energy dissipation. Default: \code{5.00e-08}.
254:     \item[\code{--damping\_noise <float>}] Relative variation amplitude for per-needle damping. The damping of each needle $i$ is randomized as $b_i = \max(0, b \cdot (1 + \text{damping\_noise} \cdot U[-1, 1]))$. Default: \code{0.0}.
255:     \item[\code{--dt\_factor <float>}] Fraction of the natural oscillation period $T_0$ to use as the integration time step $\Delta t$. Lower values increase precision and stability. Default: \code{0.05}.
256:     \item[\code{--noise <float>}] Angular noise amplitude (\si{rad}) applied to initial needle orientations. Default: \code{1.5}.
257:     \item[\code{--seed <int>}] Seed for the pseudorandom number generator. If omitted, the current time in nanoseconds is used.
258:     \item[\code{--pbc \{0,1\}}] Toggle periodic boundary conditions (\code{0} = disabled, \code{1} = enabled). Default: \code{0}.
259:     \item[\code{--pbc\_images <int>}] Number of image shells used to compute long-range periodic dipolar terms. Default: \code{1}.
260:     \item[\code{--gpu \{0,1\}}] Enable GPU acceleration via CuPy. Highly recommended for lattice sizes exceeding $30 \times 30$. Default: \code{0}.
261:     \item[\code{--progress\_bar \{0,1\}}] Toggle the visual terminal progress bar. Default: \code{1}.
262:     \item[\code{--halo\_mode \{order,domains\}}] Coloring scheme for needle visualization. \code{order} shades based on individual deviation, while \code{domains} colors by localized orientation cluster. Default: \code{order}.
263:     \item[\code{--domain\_tol <float>}] Tolerance angle in degrees used to group needles into discrete domains in \code{domains} halo mode. Default: \code{15.0}.
264: \end{description}
265: 
266: \subsection{External Magnetic Field Options}
267: These parameters define the field components and profiles:
268: \begin{description}
269:     \item[\code{--field\_mode \{static,hysteresis,sine,pulse,step\_pos,step\_neg,forc\}}] The time-varying protocol for the applied external field $\vec{B}^{\text{ext}}(t)$. Default: \code{static}.
270:     \item[\code{--B\_ext <float>}] Magnitude of the external magnetic field (\si{T}). Default: \code{0.0}.
271:     \item[\code{--phi\_ext <float>}] Angle of the external magnetic field (\si{degrees}) in the $xy$-plane, relative to the $+x$ axis. Default: \code{0.0}.
272:     \item[\code{--ext\_Bx <float>}] Explicit $x$-component of the external magnetic field (\si{T}). Overrides \code{--B\_ext} and \code{--phi\_ext}.
273:     \item[\code{--ext\_By <float>}] Explicit $y$-component of the external magnetic field (\si{T}). Overrides \code{--B\_ext} and \code{--phi\_ext}.
274:     \item[\code{--field\_delay <float>}] Time delay (\si{s}) before the active field excitation protocol starts. Default: \code{0.0}.
275:     \item[\code{--field\_freq <float>}] Frequency $f$ (\si{Hz}) for the sinusoidal external field. Default: \code{1.0}.
276:     \item[\code{--t\_pulse <float>}] Duration of the field pulse (\si{s}). Only relevant when \code{--field\_mode} is \code{pulse}.
277:     \item[\code{--torque\_tol <float>}] Relative torque threshold used to determine if the lattice has reached mechanical equilibrium (early-stop trigger). Default: \code{1e-3}.
278: \end{description}
