280: \subsection{FORC \& Demagnetization Parameters}
281: Parameters specific to advanced field sweeps and pre-simulation preparation:
282: \begin{description}
283:     \item[\code{--forc\_n\_curves <int>}] Number of minor reversal curves to simulate in FORC mode. Default: \code{30}.
284:     \item[\code{--forc\_Br\_min <float>}] Minimum reversal field $B_{r,\min}$ (\si{T}). Defaults to $-B_{\max}$ if unspecified.
285:     \item[\code{--forc\_t\_sat <float>}] Duration (\si{s}) the system is held in positive saturation $+B_{\max}$ prior to starting each curve. Default: \code{0.05}.
286:     \item[\code{--forc\_t\_ramp\_down <float>}] Time allocated to ramp from positive saturation to the reversal field $B_r$. Default: \code{0.10}.
287:     \item[\code{--forc\_t\_ramp\_up <float>}] Time allocated to sweep back up from $B_r$ to $+B_{\max}$. Default: \code{0.20}.
288:     \item[\code{--forc\_sweep \{both,up,down\}}] Trace increasing field curves, decreasing field curves, or both. Default: \code{both}.
289:     \item[\code{--forc\_rate <float>}] Target constant sweep rate $R$ (\si{T/s}). If specified, the sweep durations are scaled dynamically to enforce a constant rate $dB/dt = R$ across all loops. Default: \code{None}.
290:     \item[\code{--demag \{off,on,rotational,anneal\}}] Selects a pre-relaxation protocol to demagnetize the lattice: \code{off} (none), \code{on}/\code{rotational} (rotational decaying field), or \code{anneal} (simulated thermal annealing). Default: \code{off}.
291:     \item[\code{--demag\_freq <float>}] Rotation/oscillation frequency (\si{Hz}) of the demagnetization field. Default: \code{2.0}.
