63: \noindent
64: The collective behavior of two-dimensional arrays of magnetic dipoles has attracted
65: sustained interest in the context of artificial spin ice (ASI) and nanostructured
66: magnetic islands fabricated by nanolithography.
67: Classic thermodynamic studies of compass-needle lattices~\cite{prb1998} and the
68: introduction of First-Order Reversal Curve (FORC) diagrams~\cite{roberts2000}
69: established the conceptual tools now widely used to map coercive and interaction
70: field distributions in magnetically ordered arrays.
71: However, existing models rely on quasi-static or Monte Carlo approaches that omit
72: physical rotational inertia ($I$) and viscous damping ($b$), effectively assuming
73: an infinite-damping limit ($Q\!\to\!0$); variable FORC sweep rates further introduce
74: relaxation artifacts that distort coercive-field scaling and mask cooperative switching
75: cascades~\cite{ruta2017}.
76: We address these gaps with a Newtonian rotational molecular-dynamics model---integrated
77: by a Velocity-Verlet scheme---in which each needle obeys
78: $I\ddot{\theta}_{i} = \tau_{i}^{\text{dip}} + \tau_{i}^{\text{ext}} - b\dot{\theta}_{i}$,
79: with $I$ auto-calibrated from a rectangular blade plus a central cylindrical brass pivot.
80: Hysteresis loops and FORC diagrams are computed for square, triangular, and honeycomb
81: geometries across a wide range of quality factors $Q=\omega_{0}I/b$, and under a
82: strictly constant field sweep rate $R=|dB/dt|$ that eliminates rate-artifact
83: contamination.
84: Inertia delays switching, dynamically inflates the coercive field, and generates
85: phase-coherent oscillations at high $Q$; the resulting FORC broadening mimics
86: structural disorder.
87: Crucially, the mechanical damping ratio $b/I$ maps directly onto the phenomenological
88: Gilbert damping parameter $\alpha$ of thin-film nanomagnets, establishing this
89: macroscopic system as a transparent analog for nanolithography-fabricated magnetic
90: island arrays and providing quantitative guidance for interpreting FORC measurements
91: on nanopatterned samples.
